WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:06.400
First: Microsoft's import sample
runs twice with the same file.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.412
What happens?

4
00:00:07.412 --> 00:00:11.367
The answer is b: two policies
with the same name are created,

5
00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:14.250
because the sample never reads the tenant.

6
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.150
You saw the two POSTs
and no GET in step two.

7
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.702
Second: one library file
differs from the tenant's copy,

8
00:00:20.702 --> 00:00:22.675
and you run the sync with apply.

9
00:00:22.675 --> 00:00:23.825
What does it create?

10
00:00:23.825 --> 00:00:25.787
The answer is b: nothing.

11
00:00:25.787 --> 00:00:29.850
It exits two, and writes nothing
while any policy is drift.

12
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.275
Not even the policy
that was marked create.

13
00:00:32.275 --> 00:00:34.025
You saw that in step six.

14
00:00:34.025 --> 00:00:38.215
The module page has two more questions,
on the conflict disposition and

15
00:00:38.215 --> 00:00:42.310
on the dry run's permission, each
linked to the section that answers it.
